/-!
# Zen 2 RCP/RSQRT tables (generated; do not edit)

The AMD EPYC 7742's RCPPS/RCPSS/RSQRTPS/RSQRTSS (legacy and VEX.128/VEX.256) on one binary32 lane,
reconstructed from hardware observations: EPYC 7742 microcode 0x830107c, native campaign sse_rcp_sweep
(campaigns 066-068 of the bundle ia32-epyc-ext: every 12-bit table entry at four points of its interval),
checked against every RCP/RSQRT lane of sse_rcp_sweep, sse_random, avx_ops, avx_random and enc_fuzz
(52,794 lanes, all reproduced; validation/test/out/rcp/verify.py at the time of the triage).

x = (-1)^s * 2^(E-127) * 1.f with f the 23 fraction bits; t = f >> 11 (fraction bits 22..11).
* RCP, normal x (1 <= E <= 254): biased result exponent 253 - E, fraction RCP[t] << 11, sign s; if
  253 - E <= 0 (E >= 253: the result is below 2^-126) the result is +-0 whatever MXCSR.FTZ.
* RSQRT, positive normal x: E odd: exponent (379 - E) / 2, fraction RSQRT_ODD[t] << 11 (x in [1,2)*4^k);
  E even: exponent (380 - E) / 2, fraction RSQRT_EVEN[t] << 11 (x in [2,4)*4^k).
  Fraction bits 10..0 of x never matter; the result has 12 fraction bits (bits 10..0 zero).
* NaN: the input NaN quieted (bit 22 set, sign and payload kept) -- also for RSQRT of a negative NaN.
* +-0 and every denormal (with or without MXCSR.DAZ): +-inf (sign kept; RSQRT(-0) = RSQRT(-denormal) = -inf).
* RCP(+-inf) = +-0; RSQRT(+inf) = +0; RSQRT(-inf) and RSQRT(negative normal) = the default NaN FFC00000h.
* MXCSR: never changed (no flag, no #XM whatever the masks); RC, FTZ and DAZ have no effect on the result.
Entry 0 of RCP and RSQRT_ODD is not 1.0: RCP(1.0) = 0.99975586 (3F7FF000h), RSQRT(1.0) = 0.99987793.

Each table has 4096 entries indexed by fraction bits 22..11 of the operand; an entry is the 12-bit
fraction (bits 22..11) of the result, whose bits 10..0 are zero. Generated from the hardware rows of the
EPYC 7742 (microcode 0x830107c), native campaign `sse_rcp_sweep` (every entry observed at 4 points:
fraction bits 10..0 = 0, 7FFh and two random values; all four gave the same result in every entry).
The tables are stored as hexadecimal strings (three digits per entry, entry 0 first; a 4096-element
array literal exceeds the elaborator's recursion depth) and unpacked once.
-/

namespace X86.Zen2Rcp

private def hexDigit (c : Char) : Nat :=
  if c.isDigit then c.toNat - 48 else c.toNat - 87

/-- Three hexadecimal digits per entry. -/
def unpack (s : String) : Array Nat := Id.run do
  let cs := s.toList.toArray
  let mut a : Array Nat := Array.mkEmpty (cs.size / 3)
  for i in [0:cs.size / 3] do
    a := a.push (hexDigit cs[3*i]! * 256 + hexDigit cs[3*i+1]! * 16 + hexDigit cs[3*i+2]!)
  return a

/-- RCPPS/RCPSS: result fraction bits 22..11 for an operand with fraction bits 22..11 = index
(result exponent 253 - E). -/
def rcpTable : Array Nat := unpack
  ""

/-- RSQRTPS/RSQRTSS, odd biased exponent E (operand in [1, 2)·4^k): result exponent (379 - E) / 2. -/
def rsqrtOddTable : Array Nat := unpack
  ""

/-- RSQRTPS/RSQRTSS, even biased exponent E (operand in [2, 4)·4^k): result exponent (380 - E) / 2. -/
def rsqrtEvenTable : Array Nat := unpack
  ""

#guard rcpTable.size == 4096 && rsqrtOddTable.size == 4096 && rsqrtEvenTable.size == 4096
#guard rcpTable[0]! == 4094 && rcpTable[4095]! == 0
#guard rsqrtOddTable[0]! == 4095 && rsqrtEvenTable[4095]! == 0
#guard rcpTable.foldl (· + ·) 0 == 6481648 && rsqrtOddTable.foldl (· + ·) 0 == 11020864 &&
  rsqrtEvenTable.foldl (· + ·) 0 == 2878912

end X86.Zen2Rcp
